WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.381
"Jill took the baseball glove!"

2
00:00:18.702 --> 00:00:19.202
he said.

3
00:00:19.222 --> 00:00:21.803
"She must be the barn thief!"

4
00:00:22.844 --> 00:00:26.266
"Let's get your glove back before she hides it somewhere," Cole said.

5
00:00:27.287 --> 00:00:29.308
Both boys jumped out of their hiding place.

6
00:00:30.348 --> 00:00:32.549
Jill had already disappeared around the corner.

7
00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.970
But they could hear her calling Maggie's name.

8
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:38.932
"That's weird," said Henry.

9
00:00:38.952 --> 00:00:41.833
"Why is she yelling for Maggie?"

10
00:00:42.893 --> 00:00:46.095
He ran toward Big Spot's stall with Cole right behind him.

11
00:00:47.155 --> 00:00:51.197
They got there just in time to see Jill handing Henry's baseball glove to Maggie.

12
00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:55.658
"I found this lying on the floor," Jill said with a frown.

13
00:00:55.678 --> 00:00:58.960
"I assume it belongs to your cousin or his friend.

14
00:01:00.044 --> 00:01:02.786
You'd better tell them that this is a barn, not a baseball field."

15
00:01:03.807 --> 00:01:06.189
"You can tell them yourself," Maggie said.

16
00:01:06.209 --> 00:01:08.151
"They're right behind you."

17
00:01:08.171 --> 00:01:12.655
"Oh!" Jill spun around and saw Henry and Cole.

18
00:01:12.675 --> 00:01:15.777
"Does this glove belong to one of you?

19
00:01:16.818 --> 00:01:19.981
Because I have enough to do around here without picking up after visitors."

20
00:01:20.001 --> 00:01:22.884
"It's mine," Henry said.

21
00:01:22.904 --> 00:01:24.865
"Sorry about that."

22
00:01:24.885 --> 00:01:26.687
"That's okay."

23
00:01:27.247 --> 00:01:27.888
Jill shrugged.

24
00:01:28.876 --> 00:01:30.237
"Just don't do it again, okay?"

25
00:01:30.257 --> 00:01:35.339
"Oh well," Cole said after she was gone.

26
00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:37.580
"That plan didn't work."

27
00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.141
Maggie looked worried.

28
00:01:40.161 --> 00:01:44.303
"You'd better hurry and figure out a better plan," she said.

29
00:01:44.323 --> 00:01:47.284
"It's already time for my lesson to start."

30
00:01:49.445 --> 00:01:53.166
She led Big Spot out of his stall and down the aisle toward the riding ring.

31
00:01:53.186 --> 00:01:56.608
"Maybe we should watch the lesson," Cole said.

32
00:01:57.652 --> 00:01:59.413
"It doesn't seem like Jill is the thief.

33
00:02:00.593 --> 00:02:02.074
Or Zach or Eleanor.

34
00:02:03.034 --> 00:02:04.715
That means we need to watch Daisy."

35
00:02:06.016 --> 00:02:10.757
"Okay. I guess it's safe to leave my glove here since nobody seems to want to steal it,"

36
00:02:11.158 --> 00:02:11.878
Henry said.

37
00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:14.999
"But should we take Maggie's stuff with us?"

38
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.240
He picked up the bag.

39
00:02:18.381 --> 00:02:20.181
"I don't want anything else to get stolen."

40
00:02:21.222 --> 00:02:22.202
Cole sneezed.

41
00:02:23.323 --> 00:02:23.763
"No way!

42
00:02:24.763 --> 00:02:26.304
Put that down," he said.

43
00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.981
"Cat hair flies out of it every time you touch it.

44
00:02:31.441 --> 00:02:33.262
Maggie must have let her kittens sleep in it."

45
00:02:34.262 --> 00:02:37.323
"Probably." Henry set the bag down.

46
00:02:37.343 --> 00:02:41.104
"Aunt Ellen says the kittens get into everything."

47
00:02:41.124 --> 00:02:42.845
"I can tell."

48
00:02:43.845 --> 00:02:45.085
Cole pointed to the bag.

49
00:02:45.105 --> 00:02:47.806
"Look, isn't that a cat toy?"

50
00:02:49.307 --> 00:02:53.408
"Yes." Henry laughed and grabbed the mouse-shaped toy.

51
00:02:55.048 --> 00:02:59.671
"The kittens probably batted it inside, and Maggie didn't notice.

52
00:03:00.892 --> 00:03:04.414
I'd better stick it in the bottom of the bag so the barn cat doesn't grab it."

53
00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:06.855
"Yeah." Cole grinned.

54
00:03:06.875 --> 00:03:10.638
"That's all we need—another thief!"

55
00:03:11.438 --> 00:03:15.301
Leaving the bag behind, the boys headed outside to watch the lesson.

56
00:03:17.302 --> 00:03:20.664
They were halfway to the riding ring when Little Spot ran over to them.

57
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.401
"Hi, Little Spot," Cole said, rubbing the beagle's ears.

58
00:03:26.662 --> 00:03:28.102
Henry was looking at the ring.

59
00:03:29.243 --> 00:03:32.464
Ms. Wood was in the center with three riders trotting around her.

60
00:03:32.484 --> 00:03:36.426
"It looks like Daisy isn't here today," Henry said.

61
00:03:36.446 --> 00:03:41.148
"Really?" Cole stopped petting Little Spot and stood up.

62
00:03:41.168 --> 00:03:45.489
"That means if she's the thief, nothing will disappear today."

63
00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:47.270
Henry nodded.

64
00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:55.142
"Right! That could be why my glove He stopped talking in the middle of his sentence.

65
00:03:56.382 --> 00:03:59.324
Eleanor had jumped down from her pony and run out the gate.

66
00:04:00.485 --> 00:04:03.067
She had almost reached the area where the boys were standing.

67
00:04:03.087 --> 00:04:05.309
"Are you okay?"

68
00:04:05.649 --> 00:04:06.589
Henry called to her.

69
00:04:06.609 --> 00:04:09.551
"I'm fine," Eleanor said.

70
00:04:09.571 --> 00:04:13.114
"I just need to go inside and get a tissue."

71
00:04:14.175 --> 00:04:16.076
She raced past, heading for the barn.

72
00:04:17.017 --> 00:04:19.238
Little Spot barked and ran after his owner.

73
00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:21.780
"That's weird," Cole said.

74
00:04:22.788 --> 00:04:25.729
"Couldn't she wait until the end of the lesson to get a tissue?

75
00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:29.131
That could be suspicious behavior."

76
00:04:29.151 --> 00:04:32.112
"Maybe," Henry said.

77
00:04:32.132 --> 00:04:37.134
"But Eleanor is always complaining about how hard she's working, remember?

78
00:04:38.255 --> 00:04:42.016
Maybe she just used the tissue story as an excuse to take a break."

79
00:04:42.036 --> 00:04:43.517
"Oh yeah."

80
00:04:43.797 --> 00:04:44.497
Cole shrugged.

81
00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.398
"You're probably right."

82
00:04:47.479 --> 00:04:50.000
Henry and Cole walked the rest of the way to the ring.

83
00:04:51.496 --> 00:04:53.637
Maggie and Zach were still riding while Ms.

84
00:04:53.677 --> 00:04:55.398
Wood watched and gave them tips.

85
00:04:56.599 --> 00:04:59.240
A few minutes later, Eleanor came out of the barn.

86
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.981
Soon she was back on her pony.

87
00:05:05.684 --> 00:05:09.266
When the lesson ended, Maggie led her pony over to the boys.

88
00:05:09.286 --> 00:05:10.987
"Did you solve the mystery yet?"

89
00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:12.107
she asked them.

90
00:05:12.127 --> 00:05:15.509
"Not yet," Henry said.

91
00:05:15.529 --> 00:05:18.731
"But we noticed Daisy is absent.

92
00:05:19.871 --> 00:05:22.589
If she's the thief, nothing will get stolen today."

93
00:05:22.609 --> 00:05:25.070
"Oh! Good point."

94
00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:26.811
Maggie nodded.

95
00:05:26.831 --> 00:05:29.792
"You just have to figure out a way to prove it."

96
00:05:30.752 --> 00:05:33.114
"Don't worry, we will," said Henry.

97
00:05:33.134 --> 00:05:37.456
"Okay." Maggie didn't look too sure about that.

98
00:05:38.936 --> 00:05:44.099
Just then Eleanor led her pony up to them, so The Lemonade Detectives had to stop discussing the

99
00:05:44.139 --> 00:05:47.080
case. They all walked into the barn.

100
00:05:48.124 --> 00:05:52.206
Maggie led Spot into his stall, and then turned to put her riding helmet in her bag.

101
00:05:53.307 --> 00:05:56.048
As soon as she leaned over, she let out a shriek.

102
00:05:56.068 --> 00:05:58.630
"I can't believe this!"

103
00:05:58.990 --> 00:05:59.530
she yelled.

104
00:06:01.331 --> 00:06:02.612
"One of my sandals is
